PUT YOUR STATION PHOTOS IN THIS FOLDER
======================================

Walk the Line shows a real photo at the top of each person's chat if you put
one here. If a photo is missing, it shows the built-in drawing instead — so
you can add them one at a time, in any order, and nothing breaks.

The app matches your real station names, so the photos you already have work
as-is. It's forgiving about capital letters and spaces.

FILE NAMES IT LOOKS FOR (any of these per station; .png / .jpg / .webp all OK)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Cutting                     -> Plate cutting (Dave)
  Profile & T                 -> Profile & T-bar cutting (Priya)
  Profile Bending             -> Profile bending press (Tom)
  Dressing                    -> Dressing / central hall (Ben)
  Plate Robot Welder          -> Plate robot welder (Sam)
  SMWP                        -> Stiffener mounting portal (Jack)
  Bulkhead Fab                -> Bulkhead fabrication (Maria)
  Unit Line Deck Plate 1      -> Unit line, deck plate WS1 (Nadia)
  Unit Line                   -> Unit line WS 2-5 (Kate)

HOW
---
1. Get a photo for a station. Landscape works best — roughly twice as wide as
   it is tall.
2. Name it as above (a real shop photo, or an AI-generated one like your
   collage). The name is what matters, not the picture.
3. Put the file in this "line-images" folder, next to index.html.
   On GitHub: open this folder, "Add file" -> "Upload files", drop it in, commit.
4. Reopen the app and tap that person — you'll see the photo.

TIPS
----
- Keep each photo under ~500 KB so the app stays quick. Resize big phone photos.
- Don't upload anything commercially sensitive if the repo is public.
- To go back to the drawing for a station, just delete its photo here.
